Well this turned into another YASD.

I threw a dart at the ghost and he stepped off of the treasure pile.
I stepped on and because I had auto pickup on ended up picking up to
burdened.

In that time of course the demon appeared.  I dropped down to
unburdened (figured I could come back later).  As I tried my escape
the demon managed
to throw enough darts at me to kill me in the three steps I took.

Looking back at this I made a lot of mistakes...

1) I absolutely shouldn't have had auto pickup on in this situation.
It is too dangerous to not know what I'd be picking up.
2) After the demon threw the first dart, I should have watched my
angles much better.
3) I had a scroll of teleport, I likely could have gotten myself some
time to be better prepared in a different area of the dungeon.
4) I ought to have put the e word down on at least one entrance/exit
to the room to give myself a better chance of escape.
5) The potion of invisibility could have been useful to cause the
demon to miss and give me a little more chance to flee.

I have done plenty of protection racket runs, so this game had started
off quite favorably... I suppose that is what over confidence gets
you.

And as fate would have it, my very next character, Xyzzyx bumped into
the bones level, that now has two ghosts and ex-pets on it... :)
At least I knew enough to back track out of there and look for the
mines.  For some reason I always thought the mines could go up to
level 5... the more you know!


